---
description: File content changes must go through editor tools so keep/discard can review them
alwaysApply: true
---

# Reviewable edits

Never use the shell (`perl -pi`, `sed -i`, `ruby -i`, redirecting over files, etc.) to modify source file **contents**.

Use `Write` or `StrReplace` for every content change so Cursor’s keep/discard UI lists the real files.

Shell is fine for read-only inspection (`rg`, `git diff`, `tsc`) and for non-content ops (`mkdir`, `mv`/`cp` of whole files when renaming paths — still prefer editor tools when rewriting content during a rename).

Bulk renames: batch `StrReplace` (with `replace_all` when safe) across the affected files. Prefer several reviewable turns over one hidden shell sweep.
